<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arima Toyouji</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1569–1642</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arima Toyouji was a Japanese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daimyo">daimyo</a> who fought for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-ieyasu">Tokugawa Ieyasu</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sekigahara">Sekigahara</a> in 1600. In 1621 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogunate</a> gave him <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kurume">Kurume</a> in Chikugo province, with about 210,000 koku, and his descendants ruled the Kurume Domain until 1871. He took part in suppressing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shimabara-rebellion">Shimabara Rebellion</a> in 1638.</p></div>
